    "updated_at": "2022-03-17T10:15:08Z",
    "body": "I agree with @mikewest. When we [discussed this](https://w3c.github.io/web-performance/meetings/2020/2020-10-TPAC/index.html#h.u6tiv4d63i38), we concluded that resource-level timings are fair game, while origin-level timings need to remain TAO-opted, and network-level timings may be something that even TAO shouldn't expose.\r\n\r\nSo, I'm supportive of CORS implying resource-level timing exposure.",
